     "body": "<p><span class=\"error\">&#91;Followup from Sourceforge Tracker&#93;</span><br/>\nFollowup Submitter: sjw46<br/>\nLogged In: YES <br/>\nuser_id=1709161<br/>\nOriginator: YES</p>\n\n<p>Lynette reported the following typos against the 2.0 version of tutorial2.pdf. <br/>\nThe page references may be off a bit, but I verified that at least the first two<br/>\ntypos still exist in the 2.1 version.</p>\n\n<p>() - add text<br/>\n[] - remove text</p>\n\n<p>P18  3.  ... Also, the<img class=\"emoticon\" src=\"/images/icons/emoticons/thumbs_up.png\" height=\"16\" width=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" border=\"0\"/> can ...<br/>\nP22  first bullet   ... provides an<span class=\"error\">&#91;d&#93;</span> implementation ...<br/>\nP22  7.1.2 para 1 ... the new digital (object) with ...<br/>\nP30  para 1 line 3   ... select the <span class=\"error\">&#91;greyscale&#93;</span> (resize) method ...<br/>\nP31  para 1 line 5  ... (h)as at least one ...<br/>\nP35  7.3.4 line 1-2   ... object that <span class=\"error\">&#91;be&#93;</span> (is) the basis of ...<br/>\n  OR  ... object that (can) be the basis of ...\"</p>\n\n<p>------- Additional Comment #1 From Edwin Shin 2006-12-05 14:34 <span class=\"error\">&#91;reply&#93;</span> ------- <br/>\nI've emailed Carl for the original source docs for the PDFs. I'll get them<br/>\nchecked into CVS as soon as I get them.</p>",
