      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>The following problem was also reported by Stuart Chalk on 11/24/08:</p>\n\n<p>&gt; Also, in the SDef file for Example3 I think there is a typo.<br/>\n&gt; The line &lt;fbs:DSInputSpec bDefPID=\"demo:ex3bDef\" should be &lt;fbs:DSInputSpec<br/>\n&gt; bDefPID=\"demo:ex3SDef\" ?<br/>\n&gt; Also, is the attribute name right?  I would think it should now be sDefPID<br/>\n&gt; (or SDefPID)?</p>\n\n<p>Not that there are a couple problems.  First the PID is wrong.  Also, it actually shouldn't have that attribute at all as of Fedora 3.1.  However, neither problem should affect the ability of the dissemination to run, since the actual SDep-SDef association that Fedora 3+ looks at is the one in the RELS-EXT datastream.</p>",
     "created": "24/Nov/08 11:15 AM",
